MediaBox: m2vd times a decoder's first picture from its PTS, at any PTS.

Measured 2026-11-12 on the Plus (MPP 0986d01) with a 576i DVB-S MPEG-2
broadcast (12092 H, service 10912, top field first, open GOP of 12, two
B pictures before each key frame), through the live engine's chain
(tsdemux -> mpegvideoparse -> mppvideodec, PTS in microseconds as
gstreamer-rockchip 0001 gives them):

At 4 of 7 openings the key frame came out timed 80 ms (its
temporal_reference, 2, times 40 ms, from 0) and its second field halfway
from there to the next picture (22 s), and the next P picture early too:
both of the key frame's fields and both of the P picture's were dropped
(gstmppdec, as timed before the last shown; the live engine, as bogus),
the opening's first 200 ms showing 60 ms missing after its third picture.
The openings that went wrong were the ones whose key frame PTS fell
between 39.77 and 79.54 s (mod 79.54 s) of the stream's running time,
every one of them, and only those.

m2vd_alloc_frame() compares twice the PTS step with the predicted step in
an RK_S32, where the step (tmp_frame_period, RK_S64) at a decoder's first
picture is the whole PTS at 27 MHz (pre_pts_27M is 0): from 2^31 / 54 us
on its low 32 bits read negative for every other 39.77 s, the comparison
holds, and the picture is timed from pre_pts_27M (0) plus the predicted
step instead of from its PTS. The next reference picture, compared with
that, the same.

Now the comparison is in 64 bits. scripts/test-mpp-deinterlace.sh,
tests/mpp/open-gop-576i-mpeg2-bar.ts (its key frame 46.12 s in): without
this patch 57 pictures from field 27, the key frame's two fields and the P
picture's missing; with it 61, fields 25 to 85, each at its own time.

diff --git a/mpp/codec/dec/m2v/m2vd_parser.c b/mpp/codec/dec/m2v/m2vd_parser.c
--- a/mpp/codec/dec/m2v/m2vd_parser.c
+++ b/mpp/codec/dec/m2v/m2vd_parser.c
@@ -1197,7 +1197,18 @@

             if ((pts_27M > ctx->pre_pts_27M)
                 && (pic_head->temporal_reference > (RK_S32)ctx->prechange_temporal_ref)) {
-                RK_S32 theshold_frame_period = tmp_frame_period * 2;
+                /* MediaBox: 64 bits, as tmp_frame_period is. At a decoder's
+                 * first picture the period is the whole PTS (pre_pts_27M is
+                 * 0): in microseconds, from 39.77 s on, twice it no longer
+                 * fits in 32 bits, and for every other 39.77 s its low half
+                 * reads negative. The picture was then timed from 0 instead
+                 * of its PTS (the key frame of an opening at 80 ms, its
+                 * second field halfway to the next) and the next reference
+                 * frame too: measured 2026-11-12 on a 576i DVB-S MPEG-2
+                 * broadcast, at 4 of 7 openings, the key frame's fields and
+                 * the next P picture's were dropped, 60 ms missing in the
+                 * opening's first 200 ms. */
+                RK_S64 theshold_frame_period = tmp_frame_period * 2;
                 RK_S32 last_frame_period = ctx->preframe_period ? ctx->preframe_period : ctx->frame_period;
                 RK_S32 predict_frame_period =
                     (pic_head->temporal_reference - ctx->prechange_temporal_ref) * last_frame_period;
